To detect the presence of soap bottles in the image, I will use the `object_detector` tool from the `object_detector` library.

<command>
from object_detector import Object_Detector_Tool

final_result = Object_Detector_Tool().execute(image='path/to/image', labels=['soap_bottle'], save_object=True, saved_image_path='detected_objects/')
print(final_result)
</command>

Make sure to replace `'path/to/image'` with the actual path to the image file. This code will detect the soap bottles in the image and save the detected objects as images.

After running the code, the output will be printed, which will show the number of soap bottles detected in the image.
